[{:seon.task/name "a-unit-measures-the-work-not-the-cache"
  :seon.task/plan "seon.cost-test/the-unit-table-is-current went red for AGENTS on :db/pull-attr (11.6 KB measured, table 7.6 KB). Root traced it 2026-10-21: not the Jolt pin (the same 11.6 KB on Jolt 00a3b321 and 9e42a0d8) and not a code change. The same revision (33f6283, same binary) measured 11.6 KB on one run and 8.9 KB on the next two; bisecting over 9 revisions gave either value. The unit (seon.cost/unit-benches :db/pull-attr: pull [:note/text :note/agent] minus pull [:note/text], same entity n times) depends on Datahike's caches (:search-cache-size, the store cache) being warm or cold at the start, so the table row is a coin flip and the test flakes. A unit must measure the work alone: state the cache it runs under (a fresh db per measurement, or a declared warm-up that settles it), show the two modes are gone over 10 runs, then re-measure the row on the release binary (bin/check units)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.cost-test/the-unit-table-is-current seon.cost-test/a-unit-measures-the-same-across-runs}}
